people who live here reaching out to us and asking us for help. And there's a reassurance aspect of that, but there's also an obligation. We have a constituent services obligation, and we have a litigation obligation. What's the word I'm looking for? It's not litigation. Legislation. Legislation. There's a legislative obligation because we're responsible for that in this body.

17
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:40,775
And if there is anything, any kind of loose end we can tie up or any loophole we can close that can make it so that it's a little bit harder for people covering their faces and coming into our city and harming the people who live here, we should be doing that. So I'm glad we're taking this opportunity when things are a little bit more quiet, when the budget is done, and when our hiring is complete and when we are moving forward in the city to finish what we started.

18
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:56,654
And Biddeford, Maine is very close to here. Biddeford, Maine is a town I used to visit when I would go with my family to Maine to go to the beach in the summer. And just because it's closer than Texas doesn't mean that the people who get hurt there are any

19
00:10:57,295 --> 00:11:25,190
closer than the people that get hurt in Texas, but it does make it feel very real. So it's very upsetting. It's really horrible. We should, you know, people get arrested in Medford, too. They got arrested around the corner from where I live. It's really horrible, and we need to stop. So whatever we can do, we're going to keep doing. All right, carry on. Thank you so much. I've now shared this on the screen, so anyone on Zoom or YouTube should be able to read it along with us. I will also, on the same point that you're mentioning, say that

