40
00:19:02,198 --> 00:19:25,925
And I, look, these are basics. It's what we would always expect of law enforcement. It's what we would always expect of protecting our constitutional rights. It's what we would always expect of democracy. And I'm really optimistic that we can vote this out of committee tonight. It has my full support. For anyone who reads through it,

41
00:19:26,650 --> 00:19:51,710
It's really basic. Councilor Callahan just, I think, introduced each part and walk through the ordinance. I have no words but to say that this is just simple work for us. It's the least we should be doing right now. Thank you.

42
00:19:53,347 --> 00:20:22,540
Thank you. OK. Yes, I appreciate you walking through this. I was surprised that it is actually quite narrow. And I think that that's important to note, that it's for the purposes of our police department in Medford to be able to identify law enforcement officers from other agencies, which is very standard, common practice.

43
00:20:22,692 --> 00:20:52,375
And something that is not unreasonable at all. We're not saying, and then the Medford Police Department physically removes the officer from the city limits. You know, that's not, because that's not something, first of all, that the police chief would agree to. I've had a lot of conversations with him about, you know, a federal agency supersedes the local agency. They can't do anything like that. They are kind of hamstrung in a lot of ways.

44
00:20:52,527 --> 00:21:21,130
regardless of what they believe to be right and correct, they have to follow the laws as they're set. And in this case, at least we can say with certainty that officers should not be covering their faces and they should be able to provide an identification to another officer. And I think that's basic and simple and realistic to request.

45
00:21:22,244 --> 00:21:47,219
Councilor Callahan. I'm on already. Oh, you're still on. I'm also glad you brought that up. I read almost everything. I kind of summarize every paragraph but I did miss one and I want to assure people who maybe are thinking about what you just mentioned that it does very specifically say nothing in this section requires an officer to interfere with or delay an active law, any active law enforcement operation.

46
00:21:47,219 --> 00:21:58,238
So it's very clear, nothing in here is requesting that they stop another agency, that they do anything. It is simply saying that.

47
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:28,293
should there be any sort of question, they should be able to help a resident understand whether this is an actual law enforcement person performing a law enforcement act from an actual law enforcement agency. That that is something that they are capable of doing. And in fact, that is what they would normally do. Because regardless of how we might feel about that act, we as the government and Medford cannot say, you can't enforce the federal laws.

48
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:56,322
